3. PROBLEM STATEMENT


Student’s academic performance depends on multiple factors including
attendance, study habits, previous marks, assignments and internal assessment.


Manually evaluating all these factors can be time consuming.


The objective of this project is to create a simple program that
accepts these academic parameters, calculates a combined performance score and categorizes the result to provide suggestions for improvement.


4. PROPOSED SYSTEM


The proposed system uses a weight based scoring approach.


The user enters the required academic information and the program
processes the values using predefined weights to calculate an overall score.


The score is compared with predefined thresholds to determine the performance category.


The system also analyses individual academic parameters and displays suggestions when any parameter needs improvement. 


5. INPUT PARAMETERS


The system uses five major academic parameters.


5.1 Attendance Percentage
Attendance represents the percentage of classes attended by the
student.


Weight : 20%


5.2 Average Study Hours
This represents the student's average daily study time.


The program considers 8 hours as the reference maximum and converts the entered study hours into a percentage.


Weight : 15%


5.3 Previous Exam Marks
This represents the percentage obtained in a previous examination.


Weight : 25%


5.4 Assignment Completion
This represents the percentage of assignments completed by the
student.


Weight : 15%


5.5 Internal Marks
This represents the student's internal assessment marks.


Weight : 25%


